  "statement": "A conference has `n` talks. Talk `i` occupies the half-open time interval `[s_i, e_i)`: it is running at time `s_i` but not at time `e_i`, so a talk ending at time `t` and another starting at time `t` do not overlap. Print the largest number of talks running at the same moment.\n\n**Input.** First line `n`. Then `n` lines `s e` with `s < e`.\n\n**Output.** One integer.\n\n**Example.**\n\nInput:\n```\n4\n1 5\n2 6\n5 8\n7 9\n```\nOutput:\n```\n2\n```",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 1000 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "0 ≤ s < e ≤ 10^9"
  ],
