  "hints": [
    "The maximum overlap always occurs at some talk's start time. How can you track the number of running talks as time advances?",
    "Turn each interval into two events: +1 at `s`, -1 at `e`. Sort the events by time and keep a running total.",
    "At equal times process the -1 before the +1, because the intervals are half-open. Sorting `(time, delta)` pairs does exactly that."
  ],
  "editorial": "Create events `(s, +1)` and `(e, -1)`, sort by time, and sweep with a counter, recording its maximum. With ties, ends must come before starts: `[1,3)` and `[3,5)` never overlap, so at time 3 the count should drop before it rises. Sorting tuples `(time, delta)` puts `-1` before `+1` automatically.\n\nSorting dominates: `O(n log n)`. A quadratic check at every start time also works at browser scale, but not at `n = 2·10^5`.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
